- ``linear``: ``a + (b - a) * fraction``, where ``fraction`` is the fractional part of the computed quantile index.
- ``lower``: ``a``.
- ``higher``: ``b``.
- ``nearest``: ``a`` or ``b``, whichever's index is closer to the computed quantile index (rounding down for .5 fractions).
- ``midpoint``: ``(a + b) / 2``.

